Azure Monitor for an AKS-based application

Step 1: Enable Azure Monitor for Containers
CMD : az aks enable-addons \
       --resource-group <RESOURCE_GROUP> \
       --name <AKS_CLUSTER_NAME> \
       --addons monitoring \
       --workspace-resource-id <LOG_ANALYTICS_WORKSPACE_RESOURCE_ID>
Step 2: Configure Metrics Collection
Azure Monitor will automatically collect metrics like CPU, memory, node availability, and container restarts when enabled.
Step 3: Create Alerts for CPU & Memory
Create alerts based on metrics using the Azure Portal or CLI
Step 4: Test the Alerts
CPU/memory load in a pod using stress tools
